  "last_answer": "0e7b469de6948268aed3986628dc4830df01bbcc is the first bad commit\ncommit 0e7b469de6948268aed3986628dc4830df01bbcc\nAuthor: Yukihiro \"Matz\" Matsumoto <[redacted-email]>\nDate:   Thu Oct 22 19:39:27 2026 +0900\n\n    A boxed String's to_i parses as a typed one's does\n    \n    sp_poly_to_i_cold read a boxed String with strtoll, which stops at the\n    first `_` and saturates silently past the Integer word, where the\n    typed String#to_i (sp_str_to_i_cruby) reads `_` between digits and\n    raises RangeError: `[\"1_000\", 2][0].to_i` answered 1, and an\n    out-of-range number came back as INT64_MAX, so the answer depended on\n    what inference decided about the receiver. The boxed arm now calls the\n    typed parser.\n    \n    The test keeps to the inputs CRuby answers the same way; past the word\n    CRuby answers a Bignum, where both of Spinel's paths now raise.\n    \n    Fixes #9941\n    \n    Co-Authored-By: Claude <[redacted-email]>\n\n lib/spinel_rt.h                          |  4 +++-\n test/boxed_string_to_i_cruby.rb          | 11 +++++++++++\n test/boxed_string_to_i_cruby.rb.expected |  4 ++++\n 3 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)\n create mode 100644 test/boxed_string_to_i_cruby.rb\n create mode 100644 test/boxed_string_to_i_cruby.rb.expected",
